id: pm-qhnq6t
title: "GH-808: lifecycle completion resolver types and provenance lie when no timestamp exists"
description: "The published resolveCompletionTimestamp SDK primitive accepts empty legacy metadata at runtime while its declaration requires updated_at; it returns no timestamp while declaring timestamp as required, and reports updated_at as the source even when no field supplied a value. Correct the public contract with an explicit unresolved outcome so TypeScript consumers need no unsafe casts and provenance never invents a source."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk",lifecycle,provenance,regression,types
created_at: "2026-07-29T13:44:03.703Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T14:30:51.697Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T14:30:29.225Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T14:30:29.225Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "TypeScript callers can pass metadata with optional completed_at, closed_at, and updated_at without assertions; The unresolved result cannot be mistaken for a resolved timestamp and credits no metadata field; Runtime, declarations, docs, public surface, and packed-consumer tests agree"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: 95
severity: high
repro_steps: "Call resolveCompletionTimestamp({}) from @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.29 and compare the emitted object with dist/sdk/lifecycle-completion.d.ts."
resolution: "resolveCompletionTimestamp now returns a discriminated resolved/unresolved union; unresolved results carry no timestamp or source, and workspace memory rejects evidence-free terminal timestamps."
expected_result: "The SDK input admits legacy metadata with every candidate timestamp absent, and the result is a discriminated contract whose resolved branch always has a timestamp/source while its unresolved branch has neither."
actual_result: "The declaration requires updated_at and a returned timestamp, but runtime accepts an empty object, omits timestamp, and falsely attributes the unresolved value to updated_at."
affected_version: 2026.7.29
component: sdk/lifecycle-completion
regression: true
